{
  "_comment": [
    "Tools the adapter can download, and the actions each one performs on evidence.",
    "source.kind: 'url' downloads a fixed URL; 'github' takes the newest release asset whose name matches 'asset';",
    "  'versioned' reads a version string from 'version_url' and fills it into 'url', 'file' and 'sha256_url'.",
    "exe / gui: file name globs located anywhere inside the installed tool folder.",
    "views: what the gui opens when given a file path: extensions such as '.csv', or artifact ids such as 'hive_system'.",
    "action.input: 'folder' runs once over a folder holding every selected file; 'file' runs once per file.",
    "Step arguments may use {input} (the staged file or folder), {output} (the job's result folder),",
    "  {exe_dir} (folder of the tool's exe), {pair} (staged companion file) and, for 'file' actions, {name} (the input file name).",
    "step.stdout saves the tool's standard output to that file in the result folder.",
    "step.stdout_on_failure 'log' moves that output into the job log when the command fails, for tools that print errors there.",
    "step.rename_output gives the single file a command writes a new name, for tools whose own naming misleads.",
    "step.stdin feeds {input} or {pair} as standard input, for tools such as bstrings that refuse -f when stdin is not a console.",
    "Every step runs with TEMP and TMP inside the job's working folder, so temporary copies are deleted with it.",
    "action.pair names a companion artifact staged with the input; its args are appended when one is found.",
    "action.dirty_hive_args are appended when a staged hive is dirty and its transaction logs are missing."
  ],
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "dotnet9",
      "label": ".NET 9 Runtime",
      "framework": "Microsoft.NETCore.App",
      "major": 9,
      "download": "https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/9.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "dotnet9-desktop",
      "label": ".NET 9 Desktop Runtime",
      "framework": "Microsoft.WindowsDesktop.App",
      "major": 9,
      "download": "https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/9.0"
    }
  ],
